Comment (cmd/inline.go:332):
**M1 (logic flaw, must fix).** `activateInline` joins every view's `Ensure()` error into its result, and an activation error fails the **whole** configuration; with no previous configuration (startup) `rc.run` returns it and the agent exits. Views are content-addressed and kept by GC, so the same conflict returns after restart → crash loop. The previous configuration usually shares the same view, so "last-known-good keeps running" doesn't hold either. Fix: log view `Ensure` errors here (Warn) instead of returning them — `pluginWorkDir`/`cmd/agent.go:2268` already re-runs `Ensure` before each run and fails just that plugin's run with the clear `LinkConflictError`. Add a test for the blast radius (one plugin's conflicting view doesn't stop another plugin or the activation), and correct the docs claim (configuration.md ~L330, ADR ~L118-120).
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** **lisa implementation guidance:** Fix (cmd/inline.go activateInline): keep Activate errors (stable links) returned, but log each view Ensure error with rc.logger.Warn (plugin, view, error) instead of joining it; pluginWorkDir (cmd/agent.go) already re-runs Ensure and fails only that plugin's run with the LinkConflictError. Test in cmd/shadow_test.go: two plugins with shadowed views, one with a real dir at its shadow link -> activateInline returns nil, the other plugin's view is ensured and its pluginWorkDir succeeds, the conflicting plugin's pluginWorkDir fails with *LinkConflictError. Update the existing TestShadow_PluginOwnedViewEntries expectation. Docs: configuration.md (~L330) and ADR (~L118-120) say a link conflict fails only that plugin's run.

